  "instance_name": "audience_id",
  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community is individuals who engage in or are familiar with internet meme culture, particularly those who understand and consume racially charged, violent, and satirical content. The meme is designed to resonate with people who recognize the horror characters (Freddy Krueger and Jason Voorhees) as symbols of extreme rage and violence, and who are familiar with the trope of equating emotional venting with homicidal intent. The audience likely includes those who find humor in mocking or trivializing expressions of racial or ethnic frustration, particularly when directed at white people, and who are comfortable with the use of violent imagery to make such a point. The meme’s toxicity and reliance on racialized victimization stereotypes suggest it is aimed at a community that either supports or is indifferent to such rhetoric, and who may be drawn to the meme’s confrontational and provocative tone.",
